        "thinking": "For F-08 (extract proxySidecar to shared sidecar-client.ts), the `sidecarPost` function in plugin-dispatch.ts and the `proxySidecar` function in plugins.ts both do the same thing: call the sidecar via SIDECAR_SERVICE DO or fallback to SIDECAR_URL/bridge URL. Similarly, heartbeat.ts also has its own sidecar call pattern.\n\nThe issue is that these are in different modules (workflow vs routes) and have slightly different signatures. Let me check heartbeat.ts too.\n\n\nNow I'm thinking about where to place the shared sidecar client — it needs to be accessible from both the workflow files in `runtime/workflows/` and the routes in `worker/routes/`, so something like `src/sidecar/sidecar-client.ts` or a top-level shared location would work best.\n\nThe tricky part is that the workflows have their own local `Env` interface separate from the main one, so the client needs a flexible interface that can accept either a Durable Object namespace or a direct URL with API key. I'm sketching out a minimal `SidecarConfig` interface that lets both routes and workflows pass in what they have available, then a `callSidecar` function that handles the actual request logic.\n\nBut I'm realizing I need to look more carefully at how `proxySidecar` in `plugins.ts` currently uses the environment...\n\nActually, the duplication across these files isn't as bad as I initially thought. The core logic that matters is the routing decision—whether to use the Durable Object service or fall back to a direct URL. That's really the only piece worth extracting into a shared utility. The rest of the code is context-specific enough that keeping it separate is probably cleaner than trying to force a shared abstraction.\n\nBut I do think creating a generic `SidecarClientConfig` interface makes sense. It would let me define a single fetch function that doesn't care about the shape of each file's `Env` object—workflows can pass their config one way, routes another way, and they all feed into the same routing logic.\n\nDefining the config interface and fetch function... I need to extract the sidecar client logic into a shared module—I'll create it at `src/worker/sidecar-client.ts` and update the three places that call it: `plugins.ts`, `plugin-dispatch.ts`, and `heartbeat.ts` if it has the same pattern. Let me check how heartbeat uses the sidecar.",
